.TH MD_GET_SNR 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_snr \- query the current channel signal-to-noise estimate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

float md_get_snr(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Query the current channel signal-to-noise estimate.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an SNR estimate in dB, or -1 for NULL decoder or no current channel.
This query has no errno-based failure return.
.SH REMARKS
The estimate is derived from the decoder's delayed envelope and accumulated
confident marks. It is an internal relative metric, not a calibrated RF
instrument measurement; it may be negative or not yet representative during
acquisition. Use state or channel enumeration to test for absence instead of
interpreting every negative number as an error. md_get_channel() returns the
same estimate for a specified channel.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_state (3),
.BR md_get_channel (3),
.BR md_get_wpm (3)
